From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:40:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(cli): list missing profile subcommands; scope the
 receipt successor check

- Both `hermes profile` subcommand tables omitted commands registered in
  hermes_cli/subcommands/profile.py: profile-commands.md lacked
  migrate-identity and purge-identity (each already has its own section
  further down that page), and the cli-commands.md summary also lacked
  describe. The new rows use the parsers' help strings, and the
  cli-commands.md rows give each parser's arguments like the rows around
  them.
- updating.md said startup / gateway-status warnings and update catch-up
  all look for live successors on the current checkout. Only catch-up does
  (_pending_fleet_restart_needed). The startup warning
  (_warn_pending_fleet_restart_on_startup -> _update_owes_fleet_restart,
  hermes_cli/update_cmd_fleet.py) first accepts successors at the SHA the
  receipt's completed restart phase pulled, stale or current, so a later
  `git pull` that moves the checkout does not re-raise the warning.

Docs only; no behaviour change.

Salvaged from kvnloo/hermes-agent#89 and kvnloo/hermes-agent#97 and
rebuilt on current main.

Co-authored-by: detail-app[bot] <180357370+detail-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
